# Check out LF on every platform.
#
# framework-generator writes LF. With Windows' core.autocrlf=true git would check
# files out as CRLF, and the very next generator run would rewrite every one of
# them — showing as "modified" with no content change at all. Pinning eol=lf keeps
# the working tree and the generator's output byte-identical, so a re-run after an
# unchanged map really does report zero writes.
* text=auto eol=lf
